==Enemy==
Doge Dark is far stronger and faster compared to [[Doge]], though still pales in comparison to other Dark enemies. It gets knocked back a lot, but has full backswing, allowing it to attack again as soon as it lands back on the ground. Doge Darks often appear in swarms and can be very dangerous in later stages when their stats are multiplied, especially on higher crown difficulties, where their damage can exceed '''75,000 each'''.

Doge Dark is not too much of a threat alone, but they become increasingly annoying throughout [[Legend Stages]] with high magnifications and spam. In [[Star Ocean]], [[Marco Po Road]] and [[Umibozu's House]], Doge Dark is given a progressive strength buff.

Doge Dark drops a high amount of money for how easy it is to kill.

==Strategy==
Doge Dark is rather easy to kill in small numbers, but they can quickly kill off a horde of [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] in larger groups, and even a few can be a major threat at higher buffs. Cheap [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] with high attack power (like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] or [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cats]]) can make quick work of a group of them, but Doge Dark can kill them easily if unprotected, so be sure to back them up with meatshields. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] can instantly kill them and get extra money, though it may require [[Catseye]]s to beat stronger Doge Darks, until they're buffed to a point where you'd rather chip one down a little before sending Maglev. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] also works well for the same purpose. Any unit with a high attack rate can also abuse their high knockback count.

Later on, Doge Dark becomes a peon for stronger Dark enemies, like [[Shadow Boxer K]], [[Director Kurosawah]], or [[Bun Bun Black]]. As usual, having [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] will be essential in keeping these pushers at bay.

